// error: cannot infer the element type of an empty collection literal; give it a type, as in `val s: Set[int] = {}`
// error: the branches of this `if` agree on no type: `int` and `Set[_]`

// An empty collection literal takes its element types from the other branches or elements only
// where they have some: two empty literals, or one beside a value that is no collection, still
// settle nothing.
main()
  val c = true
  val e = if c then {} else {}
  val f = [{}, {}]
  val g = if c then 1 else {}
